 ## Background
-The concept of generalizable reconstruction from images has evolved from multi-view stereo to deep learning-based approaches. GRM (Generalizable Reconstruction Method) utilizes existing multi-view generation models to train a pixel-aligned Gaussian representation for faithful 3D generation using a single feed-forward pass [S1, unofficial]. This approach addresses the computational inefficiency of per-scene optimization in standard 3D Gaussian Splatting.
